      "side": 1,
      "message": "Answering the questions a bit out of order:\n\n\u003e Will we be able to do wasm builds in the same output directory as native? I think we said this would be possible with GN (but not CMake).\n\nYes, we can (and already) do it with GN, but not CMake.\n\n\u003e What sets is_wasm?\n\nThis is set by the gn args + `BUILD.gn` files. The samples are explicitly told to use the `wasm` toolchain. See https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/BUILD.gn;l\u003d84;drc\u003de28fc3cafb3655a19805ad714e2ccc3f905d1a5e\n\n\u003e Do you have any build rules drafted yet for FuturesTests?\n\nIn CMake, yes: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/emdawnwebgpu/CMakeLists.txt;l\u003d287;drc\u003dd85792ce64974ebe772d46315f6f671eff1430df\n\nIn GN, not yet, but it shouldn\u0027t be too hard to do. I can try to do that soon. Running them automatically will be the tricky part since we need a compatible browser. I was imagining trying to hook it such that they could be ran like the CTS tests, but that will be a pretty large project.",
      "parentUuid": "87b7fae4_847f0d25",
      "revId": "c34e8854cb7a4a214ee4fc922b4e415f38e41a81",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
